{
  "id": "selective-learning",
  "term": "selective learning",
  "definition": "Selective learning is a form of social learning in which a learner is selective about when or from whom to take in information from others. In developmental research, it is described as supporting learning from infancy and continuing to facilitate learning at older ages, especially in uncertain environments.",
