      "reasons": [
        "The packet supports that selective learning is discussed as part of social learning and that its facilitation effects are observed even in older ages, but it does not provide support for the specific characterization that the learner is “selective about when or from whom to take in information from others.”",
        "The definition’s claim about “supporting learning from infancy” through “older ages” is broadly supported, and the emphasis on “uncertain environments” is supported; however, because the first sentence contains an unsupported specific mechanism (selectivity about timing/partner), the full definition is not defensible as written."
